source: crates/hydronode-cli/tests/c3_help.rs
expression: text
---
Call any HydroNode API path with your login and print the answer.
METHOD defaults to GET. The path must stay on the profile's server.

Usage: hn api [OPTIONS] <METHOD PATH>...

Arguments:
  <METHOD PATH>...  [METHOD] PATH, for example GET /api/sensors

Options:
  -d, --data <JSON>        JSON body (or @file, or - for stdin)
  -q, --query <KEY=VALUE>  Query parameter key=value (repeat)
  -h, --help               Print help

Global options:
  -p, --profile <NAME>  Profile to use (server and login), see 'hn profile list'
      --json            Print JSON instead of tables (stable shape, for scripts)

Examples:
  hn api /api/agent/v1/me
  hn api GET /api/fleet/v2/firmware
  hn api PATCH /api/sensors/<id> -d '{"name":"Tank"}'
  hn api GET /api/agent/v1/find -q q=greenhouse
